  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring the Support for the Rohingya Refugees Affected by the Fire in March 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to contribute to reducing the impact of the fires on Rohingya refugees by ensuring access to essential facilities and lifesaving assistance. This IOM project provides 2,000 households with solar lamps, supplies 2,108 households with new LPG packages, engages 3,900 unique Cash-for-Work (CfW) laborers in debris clearance and construction, and provides 15,926 people with safe water and WASH NFI kits. The project provides lifesaving assistance to 15,926 people, including 3,691 men, 4,036 women, 4,121 boys, 4,078 girls, and 159 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
